{"name":"Adventure Isle","hex":"#6f9fb9","fetched":"2026-10-19","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"adventure","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A feeling of desire for new and exciting things.","A remarkable occurrence; a striking event."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To risk oneself. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","To risk oneself; to dare to go somewhere or undertake something."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adventure"},{"term":"isle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An island, usually very small. Compare with islet."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Obsolete spelling of aisle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/isle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Adventure Isle (Disneyland Paris)","blocks":[{"text":"Adventure Isle is an artificial island in the center of Adventureland at Disneyland Paris. It opened with the park in 1992."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adventure_Isle_(Disneyland_Paris)","wikidata":"Q2074173"},{"title":"Adventure","blocks":[{"text":"An adventure is a novel and exciting undertaking that is typically bold, sometimes risky. Adventures may be activities with danger such as traveling, exploring, skydiving, mountain climbing, scuba diving, river rafting, other extreme sports, or, importantly, any other activity that may be new, fresh or difficult and may even lead to failure. Adventure can take many forms beyond the typically described outdoor area. Adventures are often undertaken to create psychological arousal or in order to achieve a greater goal, such as the pursuit of knowledge that can only be obtained by such activities."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adventure","wikidata":"Q1436734"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Floating_bridge_Disneyland_paris_may_2005.jpg/500px-Floating_bridge_Disneyland_paris_may_2005.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.or